# GNU Affero General Public License v3 – Comprehensive Summary

> **Source:** [https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt](https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt)  
> **Version 3, 19 November 2007**  
> **Copyright (C) 2007 Free Software Foundation, Inc.**

## Key Purpose & Philosophy

> "The GNU Affero General Public License is a free, copyleft license for software and other kinds of works, specifically designed to ensure cooperation with the community in the case of network server software."

- **Copyleft**: Guarantees freedom to share and change all versions of a program.
- **Network interaction key difference**: Unlike GPLv3, AGPLv3 closes the “ASP loophole” – if you modify the software and make it available over a network, you must provide the corresponding source to users.

> "It requires the operator of a network server to provide the source code of the modified version running there to the users of that server."

## Definitions (Section 0)

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **This License** | AGPLv3 |
| **The Program** | Any copyrightable work licensed under AGPLv3 |
| **Modify** | Copy from or adapt in a way requiring copyright permission |
| **Covered work** | Unmodified Program or work based on it |
| **Propagate** | Any action that would make you liable for infringement (except running or modifying a private copy) |
| **Convey** | Propagation that enables others to make or receive copies (not mere interaction over network) |

**Appropriate Legal Notices**: Must include copyright notice, no-warranty statement, license information, and how to view a copy of this license.

## Source Code (Section 1)

> "The 'source code' for a work means the preferred form of the work for making modifications to it."

**Corresponding Source** for object code includes all source needed to generate, install, run, and modify the work, including scripts. It excludes:
- System Libraries
- General-purpose tools
- Freely available programs used unmodified

**Does NOT include**: Anything users can regenerate automatically from other parts of the Corresponding Source.

## Basic Permissions (Section 2)

- Rights are granted for the **term of copyright** and are **irreversible** if conditions are met.
- You have **unlimited permission to run the unmodified Program**.
- You may make, run, and propagate covered works **without conveying**, as long as license remains in force.
- You may convey to others solely for them to modify for you or provide facilities, under your direction.
- **Sublicensing is not allowed** (Section 10 makes it unnecessary).

## Protecting Users from Anti-Circumvention Law (Section 3)

- No covered work shall be deemed part of an effective technological measure under laws implementing WIPO treaty (or similar).
- When conveying, you **waive any legal power to forbid circumvention** of technological measures by exercise of rights under this License.

## Conveying Verbatim Copies (Section 4)

- Must keep copyright notices, license notices, no-warranty notices intact.
- Must give recipients a copy of this License.
- May charge any price; may offer support/warranty for a fee.

## Conveying Modified Source Versions (Section 5)

Conditions (all must be met):
1. **Prominent notice** stating modifications + date.
2. **Prominent notice** that work is under this License and any Section 7 additional terms.
3. **License the entire work** under this License to anyone who gets a copy – applies to all parts.
4. Interactive interfaces must display **Appropriate Legal Notices** (if the Program had them, you must keep them).

**Aggregate**: Combining with independent works not forming a larger program does NOT cause AGPL to apply to those other works.

## Conveying Non-Source Forms (Section 6)

Object code conveyance must be accompanied by **Corresponding Source** in one of five ways:

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| **6a** | With physical product – source on durable medium |
| **6b** | With physical product – written offer (valid ≥3 years) to provide source on durable medium for reasonable cost (or network free) |
| **6c** | Individual copies with written offer from 6b (occasional & noncommercial only) |
| **6d** | Offer object code from a designated place (free or paid) with equivalent access to source at no further charge – can be on another server with clear directions |
| **6e** | Peer-to-peer transmission, informing peers of free public access under 6d |

**User Product** = consumer product or anything designed for dwelling. If conveying for use in a User Product, must provide **Installation Information** (methods, keys, etc.) to install modified versions from Corresponding Source. Does NOT require ongoing support/warranty.

**Format requirement** for Corresponding Source and Installation Information: publicly documented, implementation available in source form, no password/key needed.

